    {"id":"compact-multi-head","type":"text","x":4000,"y":2580,"width":1300,"height":36,"text":"More than one checklist or departure","fontSize":26,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#172b4d"},
    {"id":"compact-multi","type":"rectangle","x":4000,"y":2630,"width":520,"height":145,"strokeColor":"#cbd5e1","backgroundColor":"#ffffff","fillStyle":"solid","roundness":{"type":3}},
    {"id":"compact-multi-t","type":"text","x":4018,"y":2648,"width":485,"height":110,"text":"Apartment check-out     12 Jun, 09:00     ☐ 2   ›\nTrain documents            12 Jun, 15:00      ✓     ›","fontSize":17,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#172b4d"},
    {"id":"compact-rules","type":"text","x":4570,"y":2630,"width":970,"height":165,"text":"Show one row per checklist. Add date and time when needed\nto distinguish separate departures with the same title.\n\nThe expanded view spells out pending and resolved. Skipped\nchecks count as resolved but stay visibly distinct inside the list.\n\nUse an accessible label such as: Apartment check-out,\n2 checks left, between checkpoint 1 Brussels and 2 Ghent.","fontSize":17,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},
    {"id":"compact-final","type":"text","x":4000,"y":2835,"width":1500,"height":95,"text":"Symbols are visual shorthand, not the only accessible status. Every row is a named, keyboard-operable control with a 44 px minimum target.\nLong checklist titles wrap without hiding the count. Repeated city visits use checkpoint identity in the accessible name.\nNaming, linking and using a checklist for a departure are proposed here; the current app keeps named checklists separate.","fontSize":17,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},

    {"id":"icon-layout-title","type":"text","x":5700,"y":30,"width":1250,"height":42,"text":"D. Icons on the indented connector","fontSize":32,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#172b4d"},
    {"id":"icon-layout-intro","type":"text","x":5700,"y":85,"width":1500,"height":55,"text":"Collapsed: one to-do icon per checklist, without a title or count. Open an icon to reveal the C1 + B2 checklist card.\nExample: two checklists between the first and second checkpoints. This is a design alternative, not implemented behavior.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"strokeColor":"#52647a"},
